112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The United Nations General Assembly \(UNGA\) is the main deliberative body of the United Nations, consisting of delegates from all 193 member nations of the United Nations, where each country has an equal say regardless of its size and economic standing. Being the most representative organ within the United Nations structure, the UNGA acts as a platform for international debate, discussion, policy-making, and reaching a consensus on matters of global importance. During this conference, delegates will address an important issue facing the international community today, the establishment of regulations regarding Lethal Autonomous Weapons Systems \(LAWS\), which refers to weaponized technology that selects targets and launches attacks without any significant human involvement. The discussion on this agenda topic revolves around the need to establish international standards and possibly an international treaty regarding the use of LAWS. The discussions in this committee will ultimately determine if the international community will be able to reach a consensus on setting standards on new technology used in warfare before it becomes too common to affect the way wars are fought in the future. You, as a delegate, will represent your country, negotiate with other member states, and play an instrumental role in crafting international policies on regulation of Lethal Autonomous Weapons Systems. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
