/P 101 0 R
/E (In conclusion, Lethal Autonomous Weapons Systems \(LAWS\) have become one of the most important and controversial issues in modern warfare. While some countries believe these weapons can improve military efficiency and reduce risks for soldiers, others worry that allowing machines to make decisions about human lives is dangerous and unethical.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E ( The world is still divided on whether such weapons should be banned, strictly regulated, or allowed under existing international laws. As technology continues to develop rapidly, the United Nations and its member states must work together to find a balance between security, innovation, and the protection of human rights and global peace. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
